      "lineNbr": 646,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002885
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-14T03:28:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I am trying to make state set as a D-Bus property for the entity-object rather than a separate object.\n\nI didn\u0027t follows the numeric sensor approach because there is no suitable redfish schema supporting this association between state and the object itself.\n\nIf we insist to put state sensor reading on state-sensor D-Bus object and that will eventually requires 2 more things:\n\n1. Association between PLDM state sensor and the entity itself, which can only be handled by case, such as the patch here:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/92656\n\n2. Most of the state-related logic has been implement in bmcweb, and the consumer simply read the properties from the interface embedded on the inventory object itself. If we try to uses the association approach, changes in bmcweb will be required. \n\nAn example is health state set, currently the logic at bmcweb simply read the property `Functional` from the interface `OperationStatus`. If we do association approach, bmcweb will need to fetch this \"state-object\" first and then parse the property from it.",
      "parentUuid": "2fcd440a_22410c1e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 646,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 646,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "a5e3f205f77fb3d5006f5490a87f7f91df91be27",
